# Canonical Turtle for the protocol-derived encoding of:
#   Benjamin W. J. Chen et al. (2023). Accelerating explicit solvent models of heterogeneous catalysts with machine learning interatomic potentials.
#   Chemical Science. doi:10.1039/d3sc02482b
#
# Version read: publisher (sha256 fdc87922ec8d52f9...);
#   the DOI above is cited, numbers are those of the version read.
# Corpus rank 116 (Application/model instance). Method identity follows
#   artifacts/kg/METHODS.md (registry: artifacts/kg/methods-registry.csv).
#
# Encoding scope: an actively learned moment tensor potential driving
# 'MLaMD' simulations of explicitly solvated copper surfaces. Encoded:
# the MTP for solvated clean Cu(111) trained on the fly, with the errors
# on configurations sampled from the production runs (Fig. 4b, values
# quoted in the text), and the preliminary comparison of MTP, SchNet and
# ANI on a bulk-water training set (runs only; errors are a figure).

@prefix rdf: <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#> .
@prefix rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
